  "comment": "Class properties — bindings, defaults, aggregation (SCHEMA.md, NORMATIVE 2026-09-27; the default moved to the schema, owner ruling 2026-10-20). A property schema 'priority' carries ONE GLOBAL default 'medium' (the Logseq shape — defaults are schema-level, not per-class). Classes Task and Project BIND the schema (sequence only — a binding is just 'this class lists the property, in this order'). A node created with Task reads the schema default; assigning Project too aggregates both bindings — the default is still the schema's single 'medium' (per-class default conflicts no longer exist). Unsetting Task's binding leaves Project's, so the node STILL reads 'medium'; unsetting both removes the property from the node's effective list entirely (no binding, no derived default). Defaults are a DERIVED read model: no property_value rows are ever written for them.",
